# MCP Tool Routing & Optimization

## SYSTEM CONSTRAINTS

NEVER call an MCP browser/scrape tool when a Tier 0/1 alternative (`rg`, `WebFetch`, existing shadow manifest) already answers the question.
NEVER take a full-resolution screenshot (`chrome-devtools` or `playwright`) when a DOM/accessibility snapshot answers the question — screenshots are the single biggest token cost in this group.
NEVER run a Firecrawl crawl/batch job without an explicit `limit`/`maxDepth` — uncapped crawls are BANNED (unbounded token cost).
ALWAYS prefer `firecrawl_scrape` with `onlyMainContent: true` and `formats: ["markdown"]` (or `["json"]` + `schema` for structured extraction) over raw HTML.
ALWAYS prefer `chrome-devtools`'s `take_snapshot` (accessibility tree, text) over `take_screenshot` (image) unless visual verification is the actual goal.
NEVER use `playwright` and `chrome-devtools` for the same task — pick one (see decision table) to avoid double tool-list overhead.
NEVER call `glif`'s discovery tools (`search_workflows`, `list_featured_workflows`) once the target glif ID is already known — call `run_workflow`/`workflow_info` directly.
ALWAYS treat MCP tool output >3KB the same as any other tool result under rule 014 (`cf-tool-result-clearing`) — clear or summarize, don't let it accumulate raw.

## Server Inventory

| Server | Type | Purpose | Config key |
|---|---|---|---|
| `playwright` | stdio (`npx @playwright/mcp@latest`) | Scripted browser interaction/testing (click, fill, navigate, assert) | global `~/.claude.json` → `mcpServers.playwright` |
| `chrome-devtools` | stdio (`npx chrome-devtools-mcp@latest --headless --isolated`) | Live debugging: console, network, performance traces, lighthouse, heap snapshots | `mcpServers.chrome-devtools` |
| `firecrawl-mcp` | stdio (`npx firecrawl-mcp`) | Web scrape/crawl/search/extract into clean markdown or schema-typed JSON | `mcpServers.firecrawl-mcp` (needs `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`) |
| `glif` | stdio (`npx @glifxyz/glif-mcp-server@latest`) | Run a hosted glif.app workflow (image/video/LLM pipelines) by ID | `mcpServers.glif` (needs `GLIF_API_TOKEN`) |
| `knowledge` | sse (`http://localhost:3711/mcp`) | Query the local ai_knowledge base (`search_knowledge`, `recent_entries`, `search_by_tags`, `list_tags`, `get_entry`) for agent/context-engineering leads | `mcpServers.knowledge` |

`FIRECRAWL_API_KEY` and `GLIF_API_TOKEN` are placeholders in the global config until the user supplies real keys — both servers will fail to authenticate until then.

`knowledge` is different from the other four: it is **local and stateful**, served by the `ai_knowledge` backend (`~/Projects/ai_knowledge`) which runs under **DevHub** on fixed port **3711**. It is the only MCP with a real HTTP liveness endpoint (`/health`), so the SessionStart digest checks it live, not just for config presence. If DevHub is not running, every `mcp__knowledge__*` call fails — start it from the DevHub UI (http://localhost:8080) before relying on the knowledge base. Prefer `search_by_tags`/`search_knowledge` with a specific query over `recent_entries` dumps (187+ entries); route any result >3KB through rule 014 like every other MCP output. When an entry here feeds ContextForge, tag it `context-forge` in the base (`search_by_tags(["context-forge"])` = full crossover history).

## Decision Tree: playwright vs chrome-devtools

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Drive a UI flow (click/fill/assert), test a feature end-to-end | `playwright` |
| Inspect console errors, network requests, performance trace, or memory of an already-running page | `chrome-devtools` |
| Need a screenshot for visual regression / design review | either — prefer whichever is already open for the task to avoid double session cost |

## Per-Server Optimization

**chrome-devtools** — config already sets `--headless --isolated` (no UI overhead, no stale profile). Add `--slim` to the args when only navigation/snapshot/screenshot are needed (cuts tool-list size). Screenshot calls: pass `format: "jpeg"` or `"webp"` + a `quality`/`maxWidth` constraint — never request a full-resolution PNG by default.

**firecrawl-mcp** — `firecrawl_scrape`: always set `onlyMainContent: true`; use `formats: ["json"]` + an explicit `schema` instead of full markdown when only specific fields are needed. `firecrawl_crawl`/`firecrawl_map`: always cap `limit` and `maxDepth` — a default-unbounded crawl can return hundreds of pages into context. For failure-driven research escalation (rule 016-cf-research-escalation), `firecrawl_research_search_github` (GitHub issues/code) and `firecrawl_search` (docs/Reddit/forum, `onlyMainContent: true`) are the mechanism — but prefer `gh` / `WebFetch` (Tier 0) when the repo or URL is already known.

**glif** — set `GLIF_IDS` (comma-separated known workflow IDs) in the server's `env` once specific glifs are in regular use; this preloads them as named tools and skips `search_workflows` round-trips. Set `IGNORE_DISCOVERY_TOOLS=true` once IDs are pinned. Leave `AGENT_TOOLS` unset unless agent-persona features are actually needed.

**playwright** — prefer `browser_snapshot` (accessibility tree) over `browser_take_screenshot` for verifying state; reserve screenshots for genuinely visual checks.

## Few-shot example

**Input:** "Check if the login button is rendering and grab the network requests on page load."
**Reasoning:** This is live-page inspection (console/network), not a scripted user flow → `chrome-devtools`, not `playwright`. Use a snapshot, not a screenshot, unless visual rendering itself is in question.
**Output:**
```
mcp__chrome-devtools__navigate_page(url: "...")
mcp__chrome-devtools__take_snapshot()              # text/accessibility tree, not a screenshot
mcp__chrome-devtools__list_network_requests()
```

## Validation gate (MANDATORY before any MCP tool call)

- [ ] Tier 0/1 (rg, WebFetch, manifest) ruled out first?
- [ ] Snapshot/markdown preferred over screenshot/raw-HTML unless visuals are the actual goal?
- [ ] Firecrawl crawl/batch calls have an explicit `limit`/`maxDepth`?
- [ ] Not using both `playwright` and `chrome-devtools` in the same task?
- [ ] Glif discovery tools skipped once the target workflow ID is known?
- [ ] MCP output >3KB routed through rule 014 clearing, not left raw in context?
If any unchecked → fix before calling the MCP tool.
